cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite both this repository and the RETFound paper it builds on."
title: "FedOSP: Ordinal-Style Prototype Federated Learning for Multi-Center Diabetic Retinopathy Grading"
abstract: >-
  FedOSP addresses three problems in federated diabetic retinopathy grading that
  existing methods leave open: (1) acquisition-style differences accumulate in
  shallow layers and are not removed by aggregation alone, (2) DR severity is
  ordinal but standard federated objectives treat it as nominal, and (3) a single
  large center dominates aggregation, so the smallest center degrades. It combines
  frequency-domain style recalibration, dual-level ordinal-aware prototypes,
  client-equal prototype aggregation, and local-step equalization on top of a
  frozen RETFound ViT-L backbone with LoRA, uploading 2.31 MB per client per round.
